  "hardware": "CPU training-label diagnostic: original Torch sets its own original CPU thread count; process and native threads pinned together to two available logical CPUs without competing scheduled workers on those CPUs. Record affinity, native thread count, actual process CPU and elapsed public time including first call, candidate/depth/aborted counters. No ladder resource qualification claimed.",
  "inclusion": "Do not replace tapes or resample actions after failure. All roots required; all tracker checks and command legality must pass on every root; every call must be documented as original single candidate or a profiled multi-candidate query. For each tape at least 80% of multi-candidate calls must complete positive depth, and require at least one multi-candidate call per tape for collected labels to qualify for the corrective comparison. Retain all rows including zero-depth or timed-out calls, no per-root outcome/depth/difference selection.",
